  "notes": [
    {
      "topic": "Counting rule",
      "detail": "Cv(strict) = N_verified / N_items_reviewed × 100% — 'Verified' means checked against an authoritative document or independently recalculated (all current Verified items are arithmetic/unit checks). Cv(conditional) = (Verified + Conditionally verified) / N_items. Gap-list grades (not in upload) and advisory industry rows are excluded because they are suggestions, not reviewed items. Items are not weighted."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Accuracy vs coverage",
      "detail": "Verification coverage is NOT numerical accuracy. Numerical accuracy was not measured (no reference dataset or measurement comparison); property values are recalled handbook/standard values with stated confidence."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Why 90–95% was not reached",
      "detail": "No network/authoritative-document access in this session, so standards and datasheet values could not be checked against BIS/ASTM/manufacturer documents. Conditional coverage shows how much is consistent with recalled knowledge; the gap to strict coverage is the remaining verification work (Sheet 11, unresolved items)."
    }
